    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels both a challenge and a gateway—like solving puzzles that connect abstract concepts to real-world logic. I enjoy the structured problem-solving but find it intimidating when it gets too theoretical or complex, especially in higher maths classes. My parents didn’t study much beyond school, so I rely on self-learning for this subject. It’s rewarding when I crack a tricky equation, though! My hobbies (like board games) sometimes make me think: maybe math isn’t just about numbers but patterns and creativity too.",
